    "note": "max_frame_payload_bytes is the PROTOBUF PAYLOAD only and excludes the tag byte and the length prefix; max_wire_frame_bytes is the largest whole WebSocket message accepted, i.e. payload + a tolerated up-to-10-byte varint envelope. Length varints are read leniently (zero-padded encodings accepted, as in protobuf), but a varint whose value exceeds uint64, or whose tenth byte carries more than one bit, is rejected."
